<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tsingoni</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tsingoni is a town on the west coast of Mayotte in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comoro-islands">Comoros</a> archipelago and the former seat of its sultans. Its Friday mosque, dated by an inscription to 1538, is among the oldest mosques still in use in the region and was later restored. The sultans later moved their capital to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzaoudzi">Dzaoudzi</a> before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> took the island in the 1840s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tsingoni.jpg" alt="Tsingoni" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: franek2 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mosqu%C3%A9e_-_panoramio_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
